  "research_notes": "Strongest dataset-specific marginal tags: H35 feature_010=1 vs 0 (+0.829) and H53 feature_002=1 vs 0 (+0.810 discovery, +0.803 validation). New conditional discovery evidence shows feature_002 remains large positive within feature_010=0 (H55 +0.780) and within feature_010=1 (H56 +0.857), and feature_010 remains large positive within feature_002=0 (H57 +0.800) and within feature_002=1 (H58 +0.878). H59 interaction is small (+0.077, interval includes zero and threshold not convincingly exceeded), so no meaningful feature_010-by-feature_002 heterogeneity is detected. These support treating feature_010 and feature_002 as separable measured tags in this dataset rather than simple proxies, though latent correlation remains possible. feature_001 positive marginal/residual claims fail. feature_047 positive screen fails. feature_037 negative screen H32 produced a large opposite-sign signed estimate (+0.804), indicating raw feature_037=1 vs 0 is approximately +0.804 in the positive direction; H32 negative claim is rejected, but feature_037 is now a major candidate for a third large tag. Registered reversed positive feature_037 main and residual/interaction refinements. Requested independent validation of H55 because feature_002 effect conditional on feature_010=0 is the cleanest remaining check of whether feature_002 is independent of feature_010. All conclusions remain dataset-specific, noncausal, and not generalizable.",
  "narrative": "I assessed all newly delivered signed discovery evidence against the 0.15-unit absolute threshold. The four conditional mean-difference claims show scientifically meaningful positive associations: H55 feature_002 presence versus absence within feature_010=0 is +0.780 with 95% interval +0.719 to +0.841; H56 feature_002 within feature_010=1 is +0.857 (+0.755 to +0.960); H57 feature_010 within feature_002=0 is +0.800 (+0.744 to +0.857); H58 feature_010 within feature_002=1 is +0.878 (+0.773 to +0.982). In each case the full interval is far above the claimed direction threshold, cell counts are adequate, and the magnitude is much larger than multiplicity could credibly manufacture from noise. I accept these as meaningful dataset-specific associations. H59, the feature_010-by-feature_002 interaction, is only +0.077 with interval -0.042 to +0.196; the point estimate is below threshold and the interval is not convincing evidence of meaningful heterogeneity, so I reject and close it. This does not prove no interaction, only that none was detected along this axis. Together, these results argue against a simple redundancy claim: feature_002 and feature_010 both retain large effects conditional on the other, suggesting separable measured tags or a more complex joint latent structure, but they do not establish causality or generalizability. The feature_001 block is uninformative for the positive direction: H60 marginal is -0.035, and the two residual associations within feature_010=0 and feature_002=0 are near zero; all reject. H29 feature_047 positive screen is also near zero and rejects. The most important discovery is H32: the registered negative feature_037 claim returned signed +0.804 (interval +0.742 to +0.867), meaning raw feature_037 presence versus absence is large positive rather than negative. I reject the registered negative claim, but I do not close the feature_037 line because the evidence strongly indicates a positive association. I therefore register a reversed positive feature_037 main claim plus residual and interaction refinements to test whether feature_037 is an independent third tag or correlated with feature_010/feature_002. I request independent validation of H55, the feature_002 effect within feature_010=0, because that is a decisive follow-up to distinguish feature_002 as an independent dataset tag from a correlated proxy of feature_010.",
